## Context

Observed 2026-11-04 from climate-finance-het (stream page 6.3, agent run on padme, headless):

- DOIfetch's default cascade missed a HAL deposit: Briera and Lefèvre 2024 (DOI 10.1016/j.enpol.2024.114104) has a full text on HAL (hal-04824002), which DOIfetch did not find.
- When the HAL file URL was given, HAL's bot check rejected DOIfetch's download, while a plain `curl` of the same URL succeeded.
- Earsom 2024 was likewise obtained only through a direct HAL file URL.

Cause not yet established (lookup by DOI vs HAL id, or the request's user agent and headers). Effect: open copies are missed, so fetches fall through to later channels more often than they should.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Reproduce on the two DOIs above.
- [ ] DOIfetch finds HAL deposits for a DOI when HAL holds one.
- [ ] The HAL download succeeds where plain curl does.
